Template: sysible/tools
Type: multiselect
Choices: terraform, vault, consul, nomad, packer, boundary, aws-cli
Default:
Description: Optional software to install
 These tools are NOT bundled in the Sysible Server image, so they are
 offered here as a choice. HashiCorp's tools (terraform, vault, consul, nomad,
 packer, boundary) are BUSL-1.1 licensed, not open source; selecting them means
 you accept HashiCorp's licence (https://www.hashicorp.com/bsl). aws-cli is
 installed from Amazon's official channel.
 .
 Anything you select is installed automatically the first time this system boots
 with a working network connection. OpenTofu (the open Terraform drop-in),
 gcloud, the Azure CLI, Docker, kubectl, Helm and Ansible are already included.
 .
 You can add or remove these tools at any time later with:  sudo sysible-tools

Template: sysible/apps
Type: select
Choices: slop, all, controller, slep, connect, none
Default: slop
Description: Sysible platform to set up on first boot
 This image ships the Sysible apps' source and installs them as containers.
 Until now that only happened if you knew to run `install-sysible` after the
 install had finished, which is not discoverable on a headless server.
 .
 slop        all three apps behind one front door at https://slop.lan/ and a
             single sign-in (recommended)
 all         all three apps, each on its own address, no gateway
 controller / slep / connect
             just that one
 none        set nothing up; run `sudo install-sysible` yourself later
 .
 Whatever you pick is installed the first time this system boots with a working
 network connection: the source is cloned from GitHub and the containers are
 built from Docker Hub, so it needs both and it is not quick. Nothing listens
 on the network until it completes.
 .
 You can change any of this afterwards with:  sudo install-sysible
